        /// <summary>
        /// Ads initial sync completed event The initial sync, ad-account discovery plus a 90-day ad backfill, completed for an ads-enabled account.  ### When it fires  Fires once per ads-enabled account. &#x60;sync&#x60; reports whether the backfill succeeded fully or partially, and how many ads were synced versus failed.  ### Scoped connects  When scoping was applied at connect time, &#x60;account.platformAdAccountId&#x60; echoes the chosen ad account when the scope is exactly one. &#x60;account.platformAdAccountIds&#x60; lists every &#x60;act_*&#x60; synced.  ### On failure  When &#x60;sync.status&#x60; is &#x60;\&quot;failure\&quot;&#x60;, the payload adds &#x60;sync.error&#x60; (raw platform error, about 2 KB), &#x60;sync.errorCode&#x60; and &#x60;sync.errorSubcode&#x60; when parseable, and &#x60;sync.errorCategory&#x60;.  ### Error categories  &#x60;sync.errorCategory&#x60; is &#x60;token_invalid&#x60;, &#x60;permission_denied&#x60;, &#x60;no_ad_accounts&#x60;, &#x60;rate_limited&#x60;, &#x60;discovery_failed&#x60; or &#x60;unknown&#x60;. New values may be added; existing ones are stable.  ### Retrying  Reconnecting re-queues the backfill and the event fires again. It fixes &#x60;token_invalid&#x60;, &#x60;permission_denied&#x60; and &#x60;rate_limited&#x60;; &#x60;no_ad_accounts&#x60; needs an ad account on the grant first.  ### When a retry is skipped  Zernio skips the re-queue only when a backfill already completed with at least one ad, or one started less than 20 minutes ago. 
