        /// <summary>
        /// Ads sync failed event An ad account&#39;s ads stopped syncing: no success for 24 hours, or every live ad at the retry cap.  ### When it fires  An hourly check covers every ad account with live ads on a connected account, on any ads platform. Fires once per ad account until &#x60;account.ads.sync_recovered&#x60;.  ### Stale metrics  Metrics for the ad account are stale in between. Use this signal to flag the numbers in your UI rather than to poll.  ### Payload notes  &#x60;adAccount.platformAdAccountId&#x60; names the ad account (&#x60;act_*&#x60; on Meta). &#x60;account.accountId&#x60; names its connection, so one connection with several ad accounts reports each separately.  ### Sync fields  &#x60;sync.lastSuccessfulSyncAt&#x60; is the last good sync and &#x60;sync.failureCount&#x60; the consecutive failed attempts.  ### Error categories  Branch on &#x60;sync.errorCategory&#x60;: &#x60;ad_account_not_listed&#x60; (access removed or platform change; check permissions, reconnect), &#x60;sync_error&#x60; (see &#x60;sync.error&#x60;) or &#x60;stale&#x60; (no error recorded; retries usually clear it). New values may be added.  ### When it does not fire  A disconnected connection gets &#x60;account.disconnected&#x60; instead, and no recovery event follows. An ad account that never synced successfully, or whose last good sync is over 3 days old, is not announced. 
        /// </summary>
        /// <exception cref="Zernio.Client.ApiException">Thrown when fails to make API call</exception>
