        /// <summary>
        /// Account disconnected event A connected account stopped working or was removed.  ### Intentional  Removed on purpose, such as &#x60;DELETE /v1/accounts/{id}&#x60; or a switch to the Free plan. Kept 1 hour (&#x60;gracePeriodEndsAt&#x60;), then deleted with no further event. Reconnecting within the hour restores the same &#x60;accountId&#x60;.  ### Unintentional  The connection broke (token expired or revoked, access lost). The account stays inactive until reconnected, keeping its &#x60;accountId&#x60;. Removing it instead sends a second event with &#x60;intentional&#x60;.  ### Immediate paths  An API removal emits at once with &#x60;disconnectionType: \&quot;intentional\&quot;&#x60;. A phone-side WhatsApp disconnect emits within seconds of Meta&#39;s notification, with &#x60;unintentional&#x60;.  ### WhatsApp reason  &#x60;reason&#x60; carries Meta&#39;s explanation. Deliberate: &#x60;BUSINESS_DOWNGRADE&#x60;, &#x60;CHANGE_NUMBER&#x60;, &#x60;USER_RE_REGISTERED&#x60;. Idle number dropped by Meta: &#x60;PRIMARY_INACTIVITY&#x60; after about 14 days, &#x60;COMPANION_INACTIVITY&#x60; after about 30.  ### Expired or revoked grants  A publish or analytics sync getting a definitive auth error deactivates the account. Publish tries a token refresh first, so the event means the refresh failed too. &#x60;reason&#x60; carries the platform&#39;s message.  ### Reconnection flags  A dead token on an ads or blog call flags the account, and the posting account sharing its token (&#x60;needsReconnection: true&#x60;). Each flagged account emits once; a later deactivation emits again, then not until reconnected.  ### Lead forms while disconnected  While a Facebook Page is flagged or deactivated, &#x60;GET /v1/ads/lead-forms/{formId}/leads&#x60; answers &#x60;409&#x60; with &#x60;code: \&quot;account_disconnected\&quot;&#x60;.  ### Reconciliation  Anything else (a number deleted in WhatsApp Manager, a channel Meta silently stops serving) is caught by periodic reconciliation, not a notification. It lags minutes to about a day.  ### Do not rely on its absence  Meta&#39;s notifications are best-effort. For WhatsApp, poll &#x60;GET /v1/whatsapp/number-info&#x60; or account health, which runs a live Meta link probe.  ### Subscribing  A webhook only receives the events it lists, so add &#x60;account.disconnected&#x60; explicitly. 
        /// </summary>
