        /// <summary>
        /// Lead received event A new lead was submitted against a Meta Lead Gen (Instant) form or a TikTok Instant Form (both pushed by the network), or a Google Ads or LinkedIn lead form (read every 15 minutes). &#x60;lead.platform&#x60; names the network.  Leads older than 7 days when Zernio first reads them are stored without this event.  ### Payload notes  &#x60;lead.fields&#x60; maps question key to answer; multiple-choice values are the option key (for example &#x60;k1&#x60;), not the display label.  ### Provenance  &#x60;lead.formId&#x60;, &#x60;lead.adId&#x60; and &#x60;lead.campaignId&#x60; give provenance. &#x60;lead.adId&#x60; is null for organic or test leads.  ### Consents  &#x60;lead.consents&#x60; lists the answer to every custom disclaimer checkbox, for example &#x60;{ \&quot;checkboxKey\&quot;: \&quot;call_consent\&quot;, \&quot;isChecked\&quot;: true }&#x60;. Route call and SMS consent into your CRM from it. Empty when the form has no checkboxes.  ### Checkbox keys  When no key was set on the checkbox, Meta derives &#x60;checkboxKey&#x60; from its text, so match on the full key. &#x60;GET /v1/ads/leads&#x60; and &#x60;GET /v1/ads/lead-forms/{formId}/leads&#x60; return the same array.  ### Deduplication  Deduplicate on &#x60;lead.leadgenId&#x60; (Meta&#39;s lead id) or the event &#x60;id&#x60;.  ### Routing  &#x60;account.profileId&#x60; names the Zernio profile of the Facebook account that received the lead, for multi-tenant routing. Always present, &#x60;null&#x60; only when no profile is on record.  ### Requires ads enabled  Needs ads enabled on the team. Zernio asks for &#x60;leads_retrieval&#x60; at Facebook consent only then; without it Meta refuses the Page&#39;s &#x60;leadgen&#x60; subscription. Accounts connected earlier need a reconnect.  ### Lost subscription  A Page can lose its &#x60;leadgen&#x60; subscription while other events keep arriving. &#x60;leadgen: false&#x60; (with a &#x60;warning&#x60;) on the Page&#39;s webhook subscription means leads are not reaching Zernio; re-subscribe the Page. 
        /// </summary>
